D = D0 exp(-Q/RT), T=873K, Q=136000, R=8.314.

Q/RT = 136000/(8.314×873) = 136000/7258.1 ≈ 18.738. exp(-18.738) ≈ ?

exp(-18.738): exp(-18) = 1.523e-8, exp(-0.738)=0.478. So 1.523e-8 × 0.478 = 7.28e-9. Times 6.5e-5 = 4.73e-13. That's J: 4.7×10^-13.</think>**Solution:**

Using the Arrhenius equation:
$$D = D_0 \exp\left(-\frac{Q}{RT}\right)$$

Given:
- D₀ = 6.5 × 10⁻⁵ m²/s
- Q = 136,000 J/mol
- T = 600°C = 873 K
- R = 8.314 J/mol·K

Calculate the exponent:
$$\frac{Q}{RT} = \frac{136{,}000}{(8.314)(873)} = \frac{136{,}000}{7258.1} \approx 18.74$$

Then:
$$D = (6.5 \times 10^{-5}) \exp(-18.74) = (6.5 \times 10^{-5})(7.28 \times 10^{-9})$$

$$D \approx 4.7 \times 10^{-13} \text{ m}^2/\text{s}$$

This matches choice J.

Answer: J
MODEL_OUTPUT_END

