**What happened:**

The HA tag coding sequence was correctly placed at the N-terminus, but the junction between the tag and the GADD45G coding sequence introduced an in-frame **TGA stop codon** immediately after the tag (the reading frame shifts relative to the intended GADD45G start at ATGACTCTG...). Translation therefore proceeds through the HA tag and stops right away — the ribosome terminates long before it can translate the GADD45G protein. The result is that only a tiny HA-tag peptide (or nothing detectable as the full protein) is produced, explaining the failure to overexpress the recombinant protein.

