Cyclohexanone + LDA (kinetic enolate) + benzaldehyde → aldol product: 2-(hydroxy(phenyl)methyl)cyclohexanone (β-hydroxy ketone). Acidification gives the aldol product 1 (β-hydroxy ketone, not dehydrated necessarily; acid workup gives aldol).

Then excess DAST. DAST converts alcohols to fluorides. With excess DAST, ketones can be converted to gem-difluorides (via DAST, yes DAST converts carbonyls to CF2). So the ketone → gem-difluoride (2,2-difluorocyclohexyl), and the alcohol → fluoride.

